 {:value "2013954"} "High Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2013959"} "Pole Vault, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031176"} "Long Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9031190"} "Triple Jump, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2013998"} "Shot Put, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2014015"} "Discus Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2014032"} "Hammer Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2014049"} "Javelin Throw, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "2014114"} "4 × 400 metres Relay, Mixed"] "\n" [:option {:value "2014119"} "Marathon Race Walk Relay, Mixed"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "63214"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "63901"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "64577"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "65264"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "65963"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "66679"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "257822"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "302147"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "359290"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19000897"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/120"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Heptathlon, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "8 –  9 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2157"} "Stade de France, Saint-Denis, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2014066"} "22 from 14 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Scoring by 1985 point tables."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Belgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/129137"} "Nafi Thiam"] " had won heptathlon gold in 2016 and 2020, and was looking for a three-peat, never before done in a multi-event at the Olympics, men or women. Only American " [:a {:href "/athletes/77882"} "Jackie Joyner-Kersee"] " had even won two golds in the heptathlon, back in 1988-1992. Thiam’s biggest challenger was Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/126308"} "Katarina Johnson-Thompson"] ", with American " [:a {:href "/athletes/150605"} "Anna Hall"] " also expected to challenge for a medal, although she was still recovering from knee surgery in January 2024."] "\n\n" [:p {} "After two events, those three were in the lead, KJT 24 points ahead of Thiam, with Hall another nine back. Thiam then won the shot put to open a 50-point lead over Johnson-Thompson, as Hall continued in third, but now 55 points behind KJT. The first day ended with Johnson-Thompson winning the 200 metres in 23.44 to move back into the lead, Thiam trailing by 48 points. Hall remained in third but was 99 points behind KJT."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The long jump saw Johnson-Thompson and Thiam maintain their positions, but Hall struggled, seemingly hampered by her knee, and dropped to sixth place, and was out of the race for bronze, as the Belgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/140954"} "Noor Vidts"] " moved into third. Thiam moved back into the lead after the javelin throw, one of her best events, and was a full 121 points ahead of KJT, an important margin as Johnson-Thompson was the better 800 metre runner. Hall ran the fastest 800 metres in 2:04.39, but it could only move her up to fifth place. Johnson-Thompson was second in a personal best of 2:04.90 but, behind her, Thiam also ran a PR of 2:10.62 to hang on to the gold medal. Vidts had the fourth fastest time in the 800 with 2:06.38 to bring her the bronze medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Thiam’s three-peat was the second of the Paris 2024 athletics programme, after " [:a {:href "/athletes/136264"} "Ryan Crouser"] " (USA) had done so in the men’s shot put. Thiam also became only the second woman to ever three-peat in an Olympic athletics event, after Poland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/115098"} "Anita Włodarczyk"] " in the 2012-2020 hammer throw. The day after Thiam’s gold, " [:a {:href "/athletes/127094"} "Faith Kipyegon"] " (KEN) would also three-peat in the women’s 1,500 metres."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1581"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/129137"} "Nafi Thiam"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {} "6880"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1877"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126308"} "Katarina Johnson-Thompson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "6844"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1586"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/140954"} "Noor Vidts"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BEL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BEL.png"}] "BEL"]] [:td {} "6707"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2343"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/150517"} "Annik Kälin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} "6639"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""